        "text_elements": [
          {
            "template_id": "subtitle_small",
            "content": {
              "text": "<strong>你知道有多少人死于次优温度吗？</strong>"
            }
          },
          {
            "template_id": "paragraph_medium",
            "content": {
              "text": "[needs translation] While estimates vary, depending on methodological differences, data quality, and assumptions about how humans respond to changes in temperature, the numbers are not small —<strong> they range from 1.7 to 5 million</strong> (<a href=\"https://ourworldindata.org/part-one-how-many-people-die-from-extreme-temperatures-and-how-could-this-change-in-the-future#how-many-people-die-from-sub-optimal-temperatures\"><u>Our World in Data</u></a>, 2024).<strong> Nearly 9.5% of death globally are attributed to sub-optimal temperatures.<br /><br />Are you surprised?<br /><br />Learn more about the regional variations behind this phenomenon in the following chart.</strong>"
            }
          }
        ]
      }
